2) what is lamda exp?
      * Lamda exp is a anonomous function.
            - anonoums means(name less) the function which is not having a name such type of name less function is called anonomous function. 
            - not having modifiers  (public, private,....)
            - not having return type
        ex :
              () -> { S.O.P ("Hello");
                   or
              () -> S.O.P("Hello");     -> when contains only one statement

        ex :
              (int a, int b) -> {S.O.P(a+b);
                        or
              ( a , b) -> S.O.P(a+b);       -> when contains only one statement

        ex :
              ( String s) -> {return s.length();}
                          or
               (s)->  s.length();       -> when contains only one statement
                           or
                  s -> s.length();        -> when contains only one statement

      Characteristics / properties of lamda expression
      1) A lamda exp can take any no of parameters
            ex :
                  () -> s.o.p("hello");
                  (s)-> s.length();
                  (a,b) -> s.o.p(a+b);
      2) If mulitple parameters present then these parameters should be repeted with,
            ex: (a,b) -> s.o.p(a+b);
      3) If only one parameter available then parenthesis are optional
                  (s)->s.lenbgth(); => s->s.length();
      4) Usually we can specify the type of parameter of compilter expect the ty[e based on context, then we can remove type[ Type Inference}
            ex:
                  (int a, int b) -> s.o.p(a+b); => (a,b)->s.o.p(a+b);
      5) Similar to method body, lamda exp body can contain any number of statements. If multiple statements are there then we should enclose within curly braces.
      ex: 
            () -> {
                        statement 1;
                        statement 2;
                        statement 3;
                  }
        * If body contains only one statement then curly braces are optional
              () -> s.o.p("Helloo");

      6) If lamda exp return something then we can remove return keyword;
            s-> s.length();
3) LAmda exp uses
      1- To enable functional programming in java.
      2- Write more readable , maintainable and concise code.
      3- To use API's very easily & effecitvely
      4- To enable parallel programming
      * LISP programming lang used 1st to use lamda exp


